Why this file exists
--------------------

ctc is a source-to-source compiler: it copies your C through verbatim and also
inserts boilerplate of its own.  Whether compiler output counts as a derivative
work of the compiler is debated, and a code generator released under the GPL
should not leave its users guessing, so the exception above states it
explicitly.  GNU Bison solves the same problem the same way:

    /* As a special exception, when this file is copied by Bison into a
       Bison output file, you may use that output file without restriction.
       This special exception was added by the Free Software Foundation
       in version 1.24 of Bison. */
